From: Shigeaki Asai <y-asai.0816@docomonet.jp>
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/jm: make every invocation of the index min/max search
 loop the same number of times

On Mali-G52 (Bifrost v7, JM), vkCmdDrawIndexed() with more than 1024
indices can get a wrong minimum index: only the result of the last
invocation of panlib_draw_index_minmax_search_helper seems to be kept.
index - min then becomes negative and the GPU reads position data at an
address with bit 36 set (page fault), or the first primitives are missing.

It does not happen when every invocation scans the same number of
indices.  As a workaround until the root cause is fixed upstream, loop
min(max_count_per_thread, index_count) times in every invocation and
skip the indices that are out of range.

Reported upstream as Mesa issue #16597:
https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/work_items/16597

This was made with the help of Claude (an AI assistant).
---
--- a/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl	2026-10-15 00:12:24.000000000 +0900
+++ b/src/panfrost/libpan/draw_helper.cl	2026-10-15 23:23:50.796770241 +0900
@@ -620,7 +620,7 @@
 #define MINMAX_SEARCH_CASE(sz)                                                 \
    case sz: {                                                                  \
       global uint##sz##_t *indices = (global uint##sz##_t *)index_buffer_ptr;  \
-      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < count; i++) {                                   \
+      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < MIN2(max_count_per_thread, index_count); i++) if (i < count) {                                   \
          uint32_t val = (uint32_t)indices[start + base_idx + i];               \
          if (primitive_restart__2 && val == UINT##sz##_MAX)                    \
             continue;                                                          \
